; FlatPPL/jax — the subset of FlatPPL that maps to bare JAX numerical code
; (no PPL dependency).
;
; JAX serves BOTH styles: jax.random provides PRNG samplers (draws) and
; jax.scipy.stats provides logpdf functions (density). A draw maps to a sampler;
; density evaluation (the unnormalized log-density of a composed measure) maps to
; logpdf arithmetic (joint -> sum of logpdfs, superpose -> logsumexp, logweighted ->
; lw + logpdf, bayesupdate -> logdensityof(L) + logdensityof(prior)).
;
; THE CUT IS SYMBOLIC vs NUMERICAL, not "measure algebra vs everything else".
; Everything NUMERICAL — every built-in function (§07), every distribution (§08),
; every standard-module member (§09), and every vectorization/aggregation sugar
; (broadcast / reduce / scan / aggregate / metricsum, §04) — RUNS directly in JAX:
; it is array math, and JAX is array math. A full pass over §07/§08/§09 and the §04
; sugars found NO numerical construct that bare JAX cannot express (verified fresh
; 2026-06-28 against docs.jax.dev — see the per-namespace audit at the bottom). The
; measure ALGEBRA (§06) is the symbolic layer: there is no JAX runtime object that
; "is a measure". Its combinators are not *run* in JAX — they are *lowered* to JAX
; density/sampler code by the §06 rules (joint->sum, iid->vmap+sum, superpose->
; logsumexp, weighted/logweighted->+w, bayesupdate->logL+logprior, pushfwd->change
; -of-variables, markovchain/kscan->jax.lax.scan, ...). Almost all of it lowers
; cleanly; the genuine non-JAX residue is small and is enumerated under
; "EXTRA-GRAMMATICAL LIMITS" below.
;
; WHY JAX, AND WHY ONE PROFILE. FlatPPL is itself the probabilistic framework (its
; own measure algebra + reification), so the Python target is a neutral COMPUTE
; substrate, not a competing PPL: NumPyro (effect handlers / named sample sites) and
; PyTensor (its own symbolic graph + rewriter, which duplicates FlatPIR) impose
; semantics that clash with explicit measure algebra. JAX is semantically neutral
; (array math + jit / grad / vmap), so FlatPPL lowers to it directly. The model
; compiles ONCE to a pure-JAX core exposing a stable inference interface
; (log_density + grad, sample_prior, constrain / unconstrain, param shapes,
; totalmass); the many Python inference packages are then THIN ADAPTERS on that core
; - BlackJAX (~free), NumPyro via potential_fn, scipy / optax, emcee / dynesty, PyMC
; (harder, needs a PyTensor graph). Those packages are adapters, NOT separate
; profiles: this is the one Python profile. (Lower to public JAX ops, not jaxpr /
; StableHLO; the Rust compiler emits lowered FlatPIR, the Python side does the thin
; JAX emission + adapters.)
;
; DISTRIBUTION & SPECIAL-FUNCTION COVERAGE IS NOT A PROFILE LIMIT. Bare JAX's
; bundled coverage is partial and uneven - jax.scipy.stats is a port of scipy.stats
; (densities), jax.random is JAX's PRNG (samplers); the two grew independently, so
; per distribution they often don't line up (verified 2026-06-28: VonMises has a
; logpdf but no sampler; LogNormal/Weibull/Categorical a sampler but no logpdf;
; NegativeBinomial a logpmf but no sampler; InverseGamma/Wishart/LKJ neither). This
; is incidental, not fundamental: every FlatPPL distribution is a CLOSED-FORM density
; (§08 / §09) with a sampler derivable from JAX primitives, so the backend supplies
; whichever half bare JAX omits — a few lines each, or (preferred) the
; reparameterization rules in core-equivalences.flatrules (LogNormal=pushfwd(exp,
; Normal), InverseGamma=pushfwd(1/_,Gamma), InverseWishart=pushfwd(inv,Wishart),
; LKJ=pushfwd(row_gram,LKJCholesky)). The SAME holds for §09 special functions:
; erf/erfc/digamma/polygamma/gammainc/betainc are bundled in jax.scipy.special, and
; the unbundled ones (arbitrary-order Bessel jv/yv/iv/kv, airy) are closed-form,
; backend-supplied. The full set is therefore admitted below; JAX is a general
; numerical backend, not a fixed distribution/special-function library.
;
; EXTRA-GRAMMATICAL LIMITS (verified 2026-06-28; §12 sec:profile-specs allows
; constraints that are not term-shape productions). A term may match the grammar yet
; still fail to lower; these are the only such cases, and they are the whole of the
; "cannot go to JAX" set:
;   1. Normalizers that are neither closed-form nor low-dimensional. normalize /
;      totalmass need a COMPUTABLE Z = integral of m — and only as a differentiable
;      function of the params, and only when Z depends on the params differentiated.
;      Three tiers, not analytic-vs-not: (a) CLOSED-FORM Z (Gaussian normalizer,
;      truncated-normal Phi(b)-Phi(a)) — arithmetic, exact; (b) NO closed form but
;      LOW-DIMENSIONAL support — fixed-grid quadrature (jnp.trapezoid / Gauss-Legendre
;      nodes), static-shape + differentiable, so 1-D/2-D normalize/truncate are IN;
;      (c) HIGH-DIMENSIONAL, no closed form — curse of dimensionality, no fixed-shape
;      integral: the only true out (plus anything needing Z explicitly at high dim —
;      evidence, Bayes factors). Z DROPS OUT when constant in the differentiated
;      variable (sampling at fixed params; the evidence in a posterior) — so the
;      unnormalized forms gradient inference consumes (bayesupdate / logweighted) are
;      always in; and the SAMPLER never needs Z (sampling is proportional to shape), so
;      an intractable-Z model can still be sample-only.
;   2. Symbolic conditioning — only the OPAQUE case. STRUCTURAL disintegrate /
;      restrict are routine: when the joint is built from a generative DAG (draws +
;      kernels), disintegrate(["obs"], joint) recovers the prior x kernel factorization
;      and restrict(joint, obs=data) is exactly the unnormalized posterior (partial
;      application). restrict on the latents gives the predictive over obs with both a
;      density and a forward sampler. Only GENERAL symbolic disintegration of an opaque
;      measure (no known factorization) is the compiler-not-JAX case that is out.
;   3. Non-invertible pushforward. pushfwd has a JAX *density* only through a
;      diffeomorphism (change-of-variables needs f^-1 and a Jacobian); a non-injective
;      or non-differentiable map has a sampler but no fixed-shape density. The §08
;      reparameterizations (exp, inv, 1/_, row_gram) are all diffeomorphisms.
;   4. Variable cardinality. Unbounded PoissonProcess — a measure over a random
;      *number* of points (§08; variates are permutation-invariant arrays) — has no
;      static-shape tensor and so no XLA log-density; EXCLUDED from the grammar. A
;      BINNED model enters via BinnedPoissonProcess / broadcast(Poisson, counts)
;      (fixed-shape) — admitted.
;   5. Data-dependent output shape. filter(pred, data) and value-dependent
;      selectbins produce a runtime-variable length → not jittable (XLA needs static
;      shapes); EXCLUDED. (selectbins over a *static* (%fixed) region is static-shape
;      and admittable; omitted from the core grammar pending a phase guard. bincounts
;      over fixed bins is static and IS admitted.) Runtime-variable %dynamic
;      dimensions that change *during* inference are likewise out; a load-time-fixed
;      dynamic dim is fine (jit re-traces per shape).
;   6. Non-numeric values. The string() constructor has no JAX dtype; EXCLUDED.
;      (Field-name selectors are compile-time — get(r,"a") lowers to static indexing.)
;   7. Soft spots (admitted, but flagged). Non-symmetric eigen() (extla) is CPU/GPU
;      only — no TPU — and its eigenVECTORS are not autodiffable (jnp.linalg.eig,
;      2026-06-28); symmetric eigmax/eigmin via eigvalsh are fine. Arbitrary-order
;      Bessel (specfn bessel_j/y/i/k) and airy are not in jax.scipy.special (only
;      i0/i1/i0e/i1e) — backend-supplied series/asymptotics, differentiable but
;      non-trivial numerics.
;   8. Precision is CONFIGURABLE, not mandated. JAX defaults to float32, which FlatPPL
;      fully supports as the default; float64 is OPT-IN (jax_enable_x64) for models that
;      request it. FlatPPL does NOT require float64 — precision is a user/config choice,
;      never a backend mandate. Differentiability gate: a DISCRETE LATENT draw must be
;      marginalized before a gradient sampler (Stan's restriction) — and that
;      marginalization should be AUTOMATED (compiler enumerates the discrete support ->
;      superpose -> logsumexp), not pushed onto the user; discrete OBSERVED data is fine.
;      Constrain/unconstrain transforms are value-set-driven and AUTO-DERIVED, centralized
;      in the core (the unconstrained log-density carries the Jacobian).
;
; aggregate / metricsum (the §04 Einstein-summation sugars) lower to JAX as follows
; (verified 2026-06-28: jnp.einsum + all reducers present):
;   - aggregate(sum, output_axes, expr) where expr is a product of indexed factors ->
;     jnp.einsum directly (the index notation IS einsum: named axes absent from the
;     output are summed). E.g. aggregate(sum,[.i,.k], A[.i,.j]*B[.j,.k]) -> einsum
;     'ij,jk->ik'.
;   - the GENERAL case (any f_reduction in {sum,prod,mean,var,std,maximum,minimum},
;     any scalar expr) -> bind each distinct axis name to a fresh array dimension,
;     align each indexed operand onto those dims (expand_dims/broadcast/transpose),
;     evaluate expr elementwise to a tensor over ALL named axes, then reduce with
;     jnp.{sum,prod,mean,var,std,max,min} over the axes not in output_axes and
;     transpose to output order. All axis lengths are fixed by inference
;     (well-formedness: same name => same length), so shapes are STATIC and the whole
;     thing is jittable. metricsum lowers to aggregate(sum,...) with inv(metric)/metric
;     contractions inlined (§04), i.e. einsum + matmuls.
;
; Assumes module bindings:
;   hepphys = standard_module("particle-physics", "0.1")
;   glm     = standard_module("generalized-linear-models", "0.1")
;   specfn  = standard_module("special-functions", "0.1")
;   polys   = standard_module("polynomials", "0.1")
;   extla   = standard_module("ext-linear-algebra", "0.1")
;   dist    = standard_module("distances", "0.1")
;
; DRAFT. Arity is well-formedness (§12 sec:profile-specs) — inference checks it before
; conformance — so arguments are written as a run of admitted closed terms (?_*); the
; profile pins arity only where it reads naturally (binary ops, ifelse).

(&profile
  ; --- top-level joint / target ---
  (lawof ?_)
  (record (%field ?_ ?_)*)

  ; --- parameters & data ---
  ((?| elementof external)
   (?| reals posreals nonnegreals integers nonnegintegers booleans unitinterval
       (cartpow ?_ ?_) (stdsimplex ?_) (interval ?_ ?_)))
  (draw ?_)                              ; -> jax.random sampler
  (load_data ?_*)

  ; --- measure algebra (§06): admitted because the §06 density/sampler LOWERING is
  ;     pure JAX. The combinators do not run in JAX — they lower to it. normalize /
  ;     totalmass / disintegrate / restrict / pushfwd carry the extra-grammatical
  ;     tractability constraints listed in the header (computable Z, limit 1;
  ;     closed-form conditioning; diffeomorphism). PoissonProcess is excluded (limit 4). ---
  ((?| joint iid jointchain kchain markovchain kscan superpose
       weighted logweighted bayesupdate truncate pushfwd locscale bijection
       normalize totalmass disintegrate restrict
       likelihoodof joint_likelihood densityof logdensityof) ?_*)
  ((?| Lebesgue Counting Dirac) ?_*)

  ; --- distributions: full scalar / vector / matrix / composite set, all closed-form
  ;     (§08). Backend supplies whichever of density/sampler bare JAX omits. ---
  ((?| Uniform Normal GeneralizedNormal Cauchy StudentT Logistic LogNormal
       Exponential Gamma Weibull Pareto InverseGamma Beta ChiSquared VonMises Laplace
       Bernoulli Categorical Categorical0 Binomial Geometric NegativeBinomial
       NegativeBinomial2 Poisson
       MvNormal Wishart InverseWishart LKJ LKJCholesky Dirichlet Multinomial
       BinnedPoissonProcess) ?_*)

  ; --- standard-module distributions & functions (§09) ---
  (%call (%ref hepphys (?| Argus BifurcatedNormal ContinuedPoisson CrystalBall
                           DoubleSidedCrystalBall Landau RelativisticBreitWigner
                           Voigtian
                           interp_pwlin interp_pwexp interp_poly2_lin interp_poly6_lin
                           interp_poly6_exp resonance_breitwigner kallen
                           breakup_momentum blatt_weisskopf
                           wignerd wignerD wignerd_doublearg wignerD_doublearg)) ?_*)
  (%call (%ref glm (?| BernoulliLogitGLM BinomialLogitGLM CategoricalLogitGLM
                       NormalGLM PoissonLogGLM)) ?_*)
  (%call (%ref specfn (?| erf erfc bessel_j bessel_y bessel_i bessel_k digamma
                          polygamma gammainc betainc airy)) ?_*)
  (%call (%ref polys (?| legendre hermite laguerre chebyshev)) ?_*)
  (%call (%ref extla (?| lu svd eigen eigmax eigmin matexp kron lstsq rank)) ?_*)
  (%call (%ref dist (?| pairwise_distance cross_distance euclidean squared_euclidean
                        cosine manhattan chebyshev minkowski jensenshannon)) ?_*)

  ; --- array & table generation (§07) ---
  ((?| identity vector array fill zeros ones eye onehot linspace extlinspace) ?_*)

  ; --- field & element access (§07) — static indices; FlatPPL is static-shape ---
  ((?| get get0) ?_*)

  ; --- array & table operations (§07) ---
  ((?| cat rowstack colstack tile splitblocks joinblocks partition reverse
       addaxes blockdiagmat bandedmat) ?_*)

  ; --- convolution (§07) -> jnp.convolve / jnp.correlate ---
  ((?| conv crosscorr) ?_*)

  ; --- scalar constructors (§07) — numeric only; string() excluded (limit 6) ---
  ((?| boolean integer real complex imag conj) ?_*)

  ; --- elementary functions (§07) -> jax.numpy / jax.scipy.special ---
  ((?| add sub mul divide neg pow div mod) ?_*)
  ((?| lt le gt ge equal unequal) ?_ ?_)
  ((?| land lor lxor) ?_ ?_)
  (lnot ?_)
  (ifelse ?_ ?_ ?_)                      ; -> jnp.where (elementwise; no branch)
  ((?| isfinite isinf isnan iszero) ?_)
  (checked ?_ ?_)                        ; -> jnp.where(cond, value, nan) / checkify
  ((?| exp log log10 sqrt abs abs2
       sin cos tan asin acos atan atan2
       sinh cosh tanh asinh acosh atanh
       log1p expm1 floor ceil round min max
       cis gamma loggamma logit invlogit probit invprobit) ?_*)

  ; --- linear algebra (§07) -> jax.numpy.linalg / jax.scipy.linalg ---
  ((?| transpose adjoint det logabsdet inv trace linsolve qr lower_cholesky
       row_gram col_gram self_outer cross diagmat diag quadform) ?_*)

  ; --- reductions, indices, sizes (§07) ---
  ((?| sum cumsum mean var std prod cumprod maximum minimum) ?_*)
  ((?| lengthof sizeof indicesof indicesof0) ?_)

  ; --- norms & normalization (§07) ---
  ((?| l1norm l2norm l1unit l2unit logsumexp softmax logsoftmax) ?_*)

  ; --- membership & binning (§07) — static sets / fixed bins ---
  (in ?_ ?_)
  (bincounts ?_ ?_)

  ; --- approximation functions (§07) ---
  ((?| polynomial bernstein stepwise) ?_*)

  ; --- vectorization / aggregation sugars (§04) ---
  (broadcast ?_*)                        ; -> vmap / array broadcasting
  (broadcasted ?_)
  ((?| reduce scan) ?_*)                 ; scan -> jax.lax.scan (direct)
  (aggregate ?_ ?_ ?_)                   ; sum-case -> jnp.einsum; general -> broadcast+reduce
  (metricsum ?_ ?_ ?_)                   ; -> aggregate(sum) with metric contractions inlined

  ; --- reification (§04) — functions/kernels are JAX-traceable pure callables ---
  ((?| functionof kernelof) ?_*)

  ; --- explicit RNG (§07) -> jax.random splittable keys ---
  ((?| rnginit rand rngstate) ?_*)

  ; --- measure-kernel evaluation primitives (§07). fromuniform/fromnormal need an
  ;     inverse-CDF; closed-form where available, else root-finding via lax.while_loop
  ;     (e.g. Gamma/Beta/StudentT quantiles). ---
  ((?| builtin_logdensityof builtin_sample builtin_touniform builtin_fromuniform
       builtin_tonormal builtin_fromnormal) ?_*))
